Bound the o2 sensor loops in fill_o2_values() to the arrays they touch.

`fill_o2_values()` iterates to `dc->no_o2sensors`, which is a uint8_t read
straight out of the logbook (`no_o2sensors` in parse-xml.cpp:872, or derived by
fixup_no_o2sensors()). Both `last_sensor` and `entry.o2sensor` hold
MAX_O2_SENSORS (6) entries, so any value above 6 reads and writes past them.

Upstream 874222b4e ("Fix crash if no_o2sensors > 3") resized `last_sensor`
from 3 to MAX_O2_SENSORS, which fixes the
subsurface/dives/Liberty_CCR_header_v1_00000011.dlf.xml case that
AddressSanitizer originally reported, but left the loops unbounded: a logbook
with no_o2sensors='7' still overflows. This patch keeps only the loop clamps,
matching what profile.cpp:1084 already does for the same field.

Drop this patch when the pinned core clamps these loops itself.

--- a/core/profile.cpp
+++ b/core/profile.cpp
@@ -1185,10 +1185,10 @@

 		if (dc->divemode == CCR || (dc->divemode == PSCR && dc->no_o2sensors)) {
 			if (i == 0) { // For 1st iteration, initialise the last_sensor values
-				for (j = 0; j < dc->no_o2sensors; j++)
+				for (j = 0; j < dc->no_o2sensors && j < MAX_O2_SENSORS; j++)
 					last_sensor[j] = entry.o2sensor[j];
 			} else { // Now re-insert the missing oxygen pressure values
-				for (j = 0; j < dc->no_o2sensors; j++)
+				for (j = 0; j < dc->no_o2sensors && j < MAX_O2_SENSORS; j++)
 					if (entry.o2sensor[j].mbar)
 						last_sensor[j] = entry.o2sensor[j];
